      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LUX AETERNA (9) is a genuine black-type performer who was too good last start, saluting at Listed level over 1609m at Menangle by 11 metres. Sure to prove hard to beat back at this level. Grand horse cut from higher cloth than this class. Likely to be short odds and well fancied. Danger can be APPLIED NZ (4) who has not raced for nine weeks. Looks forward enough for this return after winning in a recent trial and he is 1/1 when resuming. LITTLE DEMON (1) is the next elect off a last-start win by a head at this track over 1609m. SURFERS DELIGHT NZ (6) disappointed last time when tenth over 2300m at Menangle. Can do a lot better and fancy he is one well worth considering.",
